# Heroku
.env
.env.*

# NOTE: assignment.csv is currently TRACKED in git (overrides this rule
# because it was added before the rule existed). This is intentional for
# now: Heroku deploys from the GitHub repo, so the demo CSV must be in
# git for the room flow to work. Demo-only data → no privacy issue.
#
# BEFORE adding real participant labels (~20.000 firm rows):
#   1. git rm --cached klimabonus/data/assignment.csv
#   2. Remove the file from git history (BFG / git filter-repo) or move
#      to a fresh private repo, since Heroku needs no public mirror.
#   3. Deploy real CSV to Heroku via heroku-files / S3 / config var.
#
# Until then, the rule below is dormant.
klimabonus/data/assignment.csv
!klimabonus/data/assignment.csv.example

# Exports
*.csv.bak
exports/
